<title>PERU: Peru's April copper output rises 8.8 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's April copper output rises 8.8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's copper output rose 8.8 percent to 42,000 tonnes in April compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures released Friday by the Energy and Mines Ministry.</p>
<p>Copper output rose 8.2 percent to 164,000 tonnes in the first four months, compared with the same period last year, the ministry added in its monthly report.</p>
<p>In 1996, Peru's copper output rose by 18.1 percent to 483,880 tonnes from 409,693 tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>Peru is the world's sixth largest copper producer. The country's largest producer, Southern Peru Copper Corp, accounts for around 60 percent of the country's output.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
